# Tutorial-enabled Windows v0.2.1 release
Workstream-ID: lea-15
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/15
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed tutorial packaging, release publication and documentation scope
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Deliver the guided tutorial in a verified downloadable Windows release
Dependencies: lea-12, lea-14

## Purpose
Publish the completed read-only desktop tutorial in a new Windows x64 release.
Keep source and packaged usage documentation aligned while preserving private
configuration and the immutable earlier release.

## Tasks
- [x] Review the existing tag-gated pipeline, public source and release authority.
- [x] Select an unused version and align package metadata, README and usage guides.
- [x] Include the guide and first-run instructions in the explicit public bundle.
- [ ] Qualify release source and the actual frozen GUI/CLI offline.
- [ ] Commit and push only reviewed public changes with repository-local attribution.
- [ ] Publish the matching version tag through the existing qualified pipeline.
- [ ] Verify the exact hosted run, downloaded integrity files and all bundled files.
- [ ] Exercise downloaded normal GUI and standalone tutorial startup natively.
- [ ] Reconcile issue, Project and persistent backlink, then deliver the release URL.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] The version tag, package version and downloaded manifest identify one exact source.
- [ ] Both Windows entrypoints can open the bundled tutorial without private setup.
- [ ] The normal desktop, contextual guide and sibling CLI work from the real asset.
- [ ] Standalone tutorial navigation does not initialize configuration/history or start automation.
- [ ] README screenshots and setup commands match this release's capabilities.
- [ ] Private inputs, authentication, runtime history and unrelated dirty work remain unpublished.
- [ ] Existing settings are preserved and the prior version's assets are not replaced.
- [ ] Hosted publication and downloaded verification are distinguished from human/live qualification.
- [ ] The completed workstream has one issue, one Done Project item and a durable backlink.

## Completion evidence
The existing release and tag inventory contains v0.2.0 only; selected patch
version 0.2.1 without overwriting the earlier release. Reviewed the trusted-ref
pipeline, job-scoped publication token and explicit public packaging resources.
Package versions, README captions, tutorial commands and bundled first-run
instructions are aligned. Existing setup remains outside the downloadable app;
no background tracking, new LinkedIn application or invitation is authorized.
Hosted source/frozen qualification, publication and downloaded native verification
are pending, not established by the earlier source tutorial checks.
The first fresh full source gate passed lint, format and typing, then failed
with a Windows access violation/native heap-corruption exit after test
assertions. The non-GUI selection exits normally; GUI lifetime isolation and
correction are required before source qualification or publication is claimed.
GUI diagnostics found retained closed windows. A focused shutdown regression
failed before the correction: the standalone tutorial was not destroyed when
its event loop returned. Desktop startup now explicitly delivers owned-window
deletion before application shutdown; Qt fixtures share one session application
and clean up native widgets. The corrected full local gates passed Ruff,
Black and product typing, then 698 tests with exit zero and no retained
top-level Qt widgets. The unrelated untracked plugin was excluded from local
lint and remains unpublished. Frozen and downloaded qualification is pending.

